      "writtenOn": "2024-01-13T07:24:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree. I converted it to the error message.\n\nThe `android_work` function will execute on the worker thread. From my understanding, the work function that will run on the worker thread does not need to return an error. Ideally, errors should be handled gracefully and resources should be released. In our case, whenever an error occurs, I am logging the error. Since I do not have any resources, I have not performed any resource-related actions.\n\nI have checked the other instances which are doing the similar behavior. For example: [hub.c](https://source.corp.google.com/h/android/kernel/superproject/+/common-android-mainline:common/drivers/usb/core/hub.c;l\u003d839;drc\u003d14a91ec64347dee6a4f33f0033e77e2b2ee8d57c?q\u003dINIT_WORK\u0026ss\u003dh%2Fandroid%2Fkernel%2Fsuperproject%2F%2B%2Frefs%2Fheads%2Fcommon-android-mainline:common%2Fdrivers%2Fusb%2F\u0026start\u003d1)",
